## Cold boot

The user explicitly approved BOOT-only flashing and reboot. Every flash command
was serial-gated and targeted `boot` only, mapped through sysfs PARTNAME to
/dev/mmcblk0p7 (10MiB). The complete partition was read back before reboot and
its candidate-length prefix matched the image byte-for-byte. Commands:
  fastboot -s 00001EB100006FAB flash boot boot-fixed.img
  fastboot -s 00001EB100006FAB oem cat:/dev/mmcblk0p7
  fastboot -s 00001EB100006FAB get_staged fixed-readback.img
  fastboot -s 00001EB100006FAB reboot

No agent command wrote aboot, recovery, system or userdata. The original BOOT
backup remains in target/expressltexx-lab/20260930-inventory/boot-before.img,
verified by two identical reads before the first flash, SHA256
5b42e21d005d963ad969cd3b8d5f632f221ee84753c4218614caf41092084d73.
Rollback was not exercised. No UART port was taken over.

Before this fix, AUTO_ZRELADDR selected80008000 from the PC while the appended
DTB branch skipped validation until after cache setup. The clean UART-command-
line boot restored RAM beginning80200000 but still lacked a Kernel code
resource there; SoC ID0 was observed through ADB. The fixed configuration
establishes ZRELADDR80208000 before cache setup (initial page directory80204000)
and the real cold boot then showed Kernel code80208000 and SoC ID116. This is
separate from aboot's mem=100M fallback, fixed in fa07759.

