## Two consecutive actual kexec handoffs

Destination images differ from their underlying boot image ONLY in the header
command line, adding vmalloc=0x1D600000, pocketboot.log=info and a unique
pocketboot.handoff marker. Kernel/DTB/initramfs bytes are unchanged. The markers
were not flashed to BOOT, so a reset to the persistent image cannot satisfy
these destination assertions.

1. Fixed-address cold kernel -> automatic-address CI kernel:
   fastboot -s 00001EB100006FAB boot handoff-auto.img
   USB target returned after ~3.4s; ADB showed the CI kernel build, unique marker,
