Both destination kernels were UP. This is Pocketboot-to-Pocketboot validation,
not a distinct distribution boot or SMP-destination result. USB, eMMC and input
devices enumerated; physical display/touch behavior and external SD were not
validated. Expressatt was not touched.

Known retained log limitations: the two-CPU DT emits a max-cores1 warning under
the UP loader; maxtouch.cfg is absent but the touchscreen registers; MMCC reports
sync_state pending on disabled/unbound display/GPU paths; no boot entries were
found. These observations are not hidden by a blanket 'all hardware works' claim.

