## Workspace restoration and post-restore verification

After the second handoff the workspace was externally replaced with an empty
checkout and a new .git file. The complete prior directory survived as the
adjacent pocketboot~. No cause is asserted; the timing alone does not establish
whether the Delta update/restart caused it.

With explicit user approval:
  rsync -a --ignore-existing --exclude='/.git' ../pocketboot~/ ./
No deletion or overwrite option was used. The new .git stayed byte-identical,
and the source directory was left intact. All156 tracked files (including modes)
matched the preserved tree; all63 preserved lab files matched by SHA256. Only
three intended config/test/guide files differed from already-published fa07759.
The clone HEAD/index were advanced to that already-published descendant without
checking out/overwriting files. Validation wording was then updated in the two
guides to record the measured scope and matching fixed-ZRELADDR requirement.

